# Codex Loom — Cline Working Rules

## Project Identity

Codex Loom compiles YAML item definitions into Velvet Lattice story card format for AI Dungeon scenarios.

## Branch / Version Context

- Active work is the **v4 rebuild on `v4-phase1`**. Phases 1–7 are complete; Phase 8 is next.
- **`sections:` is the only component grammar.** v3 syntaxes (`src/pe.js`, `src/description.js`, `src/opening.js`) no longer exist.
- A component is a named mapping of sections, and every component type — Plot Essentials, AI Instructions, Author's Note, Opening, Description — reads the same way.

## Testing

- Run: `npm test` (Jest). Targets `test:unit`, `test:integration`, `test:coverage` also available.
- `npm run compile` compiles `test/compile.yaml` as a smoke check.
- **A passing suite is "done" for code changes.**

##  Pathological Fixtures

- `__tests__/fixtures/pathological/` freezes diagnostic output (code, severity, file, message).
- It is authored from the spec. If the compiler disagrees, the fixture pins the disagreement rather than being edited to match.

## Line Endings Are Load-Bearing

- `.gitattributes` pins `__tests__/fixtures/**` and `test/**` to `eol=lf`.
- CRLF conversion adds bytes per line and breaks character-count assertions in the pathological snapshot (CL0710 / CL0711 compare opening lengths against the 4,000-character cap).
- If fixture assertions fail by a handful of characters on a fresh clone, check this before suspecting the compiler.

## Working Norms

- Confirm scope before touching files. List every file you will modify and flag anything out of scope or in live/published folders; wait for approval.
- If disagreeing with an approach, make the case once concretely, then yield if the preference is restated. A second round is for factual errors or real risk only.
- Stay on the ask; no unsolicited analysis of the user.

## Session Recaps

- Use the `wrap` skill for in-session wrap-up and session recaps.
- Write session recaps directly to: `C:\Users\blues\Vault\4 Code\4.3.11 AID Tools - Codex Loom\0 System\03 Records`
- Author in session recaps is your model name (ex: `Kimi 2.6`, `Qwen 3.8`)
